runch, Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Southern","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"wqGkMLZVXc0pYVjr3zDrpA","review_id":"7w_EoeDL0IfObXVQjmxzRw","date":"2012-10-01T16:54:20","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.939615786075592,"text_excerpt":"Service was great. Our waitress was awesome. I forget her name but she was hilarious and gave great food recommendations. I love it when a waitstaff really knows their menu! She also got us a great Sazerac. We ordered alligator bites which were delicious.. much better than the ones we had earlier at Pat O'Briens. I had the spinach salad with bacon vinaigrette and the pork belly and it was SO good. The dressing was amazing. I wish I could take it home and eat it with everything! My husband had the Crawfish Etoufée and he ate it up in literally 5 minutes. We've seen it out on menus since then but we have not had the nerve to order it because we don't want it to ruin our experience of the on..."},{"business_id":"wqGkMLZVXc0pYVjr3zDrpA","review_id":"4R6JkhqGc8I85MkndKjjqQ","date":"2012-03-12T16:02:14","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9356194138526917,"text_excerpt":"Went here on a quiet night mid week. Walked through the bar/cafe in the front(which was very crowded) to the well appointed dining room in the back. We sat at a corner table and were the only diners in the restaurant. The waiter promptly arrived and brought menus. I had a glass of wine from a very reasonable wine list and my companion a beer. I ordered of the special which was basically a tasting of three creole specialties.My companion ordered another special that was a dumpling casserole dish. I loved mine,and my comp said he liked the dumpling dish! We dined through the length of the meal as the only ones in the restaurant and found it very pleasant and romantic, actually. Another coup..."},{"business_id":"wqGkMLZVXc0pYVjr3zDrpA","review_id":"RymW_WIByR_fnd3Wi_DboA","date":"2012-10-20T12:59:37","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.932386577129364,"text_excerpt":"This place is a definite winner! I am very skeptical of hotel restaurants. This one is in the Hotel St. Marie in the French Quarter. Some friends insisted we go eat there. The atmosphere was wonderful. Very light, typical New Orleans type decor and design without the dark and dust found in some New Orleans restaurants. They had inside and outside seating. We sat outside in the Courtyard on this beautiful unseasonally cool October night. The staff was prompt, professional and pleasant. We started off with the shrimp and avocado cerviche. The avocado was ripe to perfection. It was like butter when you put it in your mouth. The seasoning was perfect, and represented the best of Americanized ..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"wqGkMLZVXc0pYVjr3zDrpA","photo_id":"gIrM6Fyv_roqwKovCObD7A","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/gIrM6Fyv_roqwKovCObD7A.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9102427363395691},{"business_id":"wqGkMLZVXc0pYVjr3zDrpA","photo_id":"mx_y9DxAEilq4n